\par\par \b \uc2  Taiwan dlr ends sharply down on China/Japan$ worry. \b0\par\par\uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 1998\par 10:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TAIPEI, Aug 10 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar ended sharply lower on Monday as investors, spooked by mounting concerns about depreciation pressure on the Hong Kong dollar, China's yuan and Japan's yen sought a safe haven in the greenback, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As in recent sessions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deliberately pushed the unit up at the open, setting a benchmark at T$34.453. Investors responded as they have most every day, actively buying U.S. dollars to drag the Taiwan dollar back below T$34.6. \par \par \uc2  As jitters over possible declines of the Hong Kong dollar and China's yuan showed no signs of abating, the local unit continued to head south before closing at T$34.781. \par \par \uc2  Monday's T$34.781 close - the lowest since a closing low of T$34.819 marked on June 16 - was sharply lower than Friday's T$34.6 finish. \par \par \uc2  Monday's intraday low of T$34.80 was the lowest since an intraday low of T$34.839 set on June 17. \par \par \uc2  Turnover through dealers was active at US$243.5 million. \par \par \uc2  A weak Japanese yen also dampened sentiment. Japan's yen was trading weaker at below the 146 level to U.S. dollar in Tokyo trade, compared with late Friday's 145.53-55. \par \par \uc2  "Many investors are simply panicked. The outlook for the Taiwan dollar seems gloomy," one bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said persistent pressure on the Hong Kong dollar and China's renminbi yuan was fuelling demand for the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "Devaluation pressure on the Hong Kong dollar and China's renminbi is mounting. How can the Taiwan dollar be immune?" another dealer asked. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  waded into the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid fears that Beijing may devalue the yuan - the third time since July 31 that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's black market U.S. dollar rate has spiked above nine yuan per dollar, against an official rate of around 8.28. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have tolerated wider fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the local unit's downtrend, but it did not try to buck the trend," the first dealer said. "Maybe it felt it could not resist the trend, may be it felt depreciation will help exports," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Shea Jia-dong has vowed to maintain the Taiwan dollar's stability, saying on Sunday Taiwan would not join a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation race. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do its best to maintain stability of the Taiwan dollar and will not join a competition of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation," Taiwan newspapers quoted Shea as telling U.S. finance and Federal Reserve officials in Washington. \par \par \uc2  "We know what role we should play," added Shea, who was in the United States to attend the vice-ministerial level trade talks between Washington and Taipei. \par \par \uc2  On Taiwan's second market, Cosmos \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which opened lower at T$34.714, closed at T$34.799 against Friday's T$34.635 finish. The local unit traded between T$34.695-799. \par \par \uc2     Dealers said they expected the Taiwan dollar to test T$35 in \par \par \uc2   the near term. \par \par \uc2     ((Taipei newsroom, +886 2 2508-0815 fax +886 2 2508-0204, \par \par \uc2  taipei.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8a02rxg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
