\par\par \b \uc2  China seen holding off yuan devaluation - for now. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Bill Savadove \par \uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 1998\par 06:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 9 (Reuters) - China is expected to stave off a devaluation of its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the end of this year but pressure is mounting as the Japanese yen wobbles. \par \par \uc2  China's top leaders have vowed repeatedly to keep the yuan stable, since a devaluation could spark a new round of falls in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and impact even the world economy. \par \par \uc2  But they have also hinted that Beijing's will to resist a devaluation depends on Japan's ability to keep the yen from depreciating further. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar hit a two-month high at 146.25 yen on Friday and stood within striking distance of its eight year high at 146.75 reached on June 16. \par \par \uc2  In Hong Kong, a special administrative region of China, the Hong Kong dollar came under attack last week as speculators bet on a future yuan devaluation. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday for the second time in a week to support the yuan and soothe twitchy sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Bankers and Chinese officials said economic fundamentals and political necessity argued against a devaluation for now. \par \par \uc2  "In terms of current economic fundamentals, it still looks pretty good," said a foreign banker, who declined to be named. \par \par \uc2  "The real question is how long that's going to last if the rest of Asia continues to be in the doldrums." \par \par \uc2  The Asian turmoil has already started to hurt. \par \par \uc2  China's gross domestic product rose seven percent year-on-year in the first half of this year, below the eight percent target for all of 1998 which Beijing has set to absorb workers laid off from failing state enterprises. \par \par \uc2  But a war chest of $140.51 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at end-June and a trade surplus of $22.5 billion in the first half still provided a cushion against a devaluation, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The pressure for a devaluation is clearly intense but I still think the Chinese government has the ability to defend the yuan, at least for this year," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer. \par \par \uc2  China's own citizens and international investors are not so sure about the government's will to hold the yuan stable. \par \par \uc2  In Shanghai, the black market rate for U.S. dollars spiked last week to over nine yuan per dollar, against an official rate of around 8.28, street dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Chinese officials played down the black market frenzy. \par \par \uc2  "The leaders have emphasised many times that under a normal situation, the yuan will not be devalued," said an official of the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  System, the tightly controlled national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "If in the second half of next year the balance-of-payments is poor, then it may have to be considered." \par \par \uc2  The political costs of a devaluation would be high. \par \par \uc2  China would not only lose face on the world stage by breaking a pledge, but could also set off a fresh round of depreciation in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and upset the stability of the Hong Kong dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Social stability at home would also come under threat as the value of people's savings fell overnight and imported inflation pushed prices up, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep the yuan stable at around 8.28 to the U.S. dollar in the short term, and a fall below that key level would mark a shift in policy. \par \par \uc2  "If 8.28 is not broken that means the government is still determined to defend the yuan," one dealer said. "If they want to devalue they have to give up that level first." \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8902r2m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
