\par\par \b \uc2  Economic woes spur heavy HK dlr sales - analysts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrea Ricci \par \uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 13:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Aug 6 (Reuters) - Poor economic fundamentals were encouraging the heavy sales of Hong Kong dollars that have unnerved \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the territory and throughout Asia, dealers and analysts said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "We had expected earlier that speculative attacks against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would come in August on the release of poor economic data and earnings results," Andrew Fung, treasurer at Commonwealth Bank of Australia, said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investment banks as well as some funds are thought to have sold some US$3 billion in spot Hong Kong dollars and US$2 billion in forward contracts on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the volume of selling slackened, with some US$1.5 billion sold in the spot market and US$1 billion in the forward market, said Frank Gong, vice president, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, Asia, at Bank of America in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  At least four major U.S. investment banks reportedly were dealing directly in the market rather than through intermediaries, selling short the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both the spot and forward market. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers suspected it was a coordinated effort. \par \par \uc2  "It seems that they know what the others are doing and they are coming out using their own names at the same time," a chief dealer at a major bank said. \par \par \uc2  The hefty sales of Hong Kong dollars began before the Hong Kong market opened on Wednesday and came despite a strengthening of the yen. Over the past several weeks, Hong Kong dollar forwards and interest rates have risen as the yen falls. \par \par \uc2  But CBA's Fung said the sales were sparked by worries about Hong Kong's domestic economy. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese yen is an external factor, while the poor local economic figures reflects the weak fundamentals of the local economy," Fung said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong goverment on Monday revealed that the economy contracted 2.8 percent in the first quarter of this year, worse than the two percent decline forecast in May. \par \par \uc2  Second quarter data are expected to be even worse and a full-year recession, the first-ever recorded, is on the cards. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index on Thursday ended at its lowest level since January 1995, down 2.84 percent at 7,254.36. \par \par \uc2  US/HK forwards with maturities over three months have risen by more than 500 points over the past two days, while the Hong Kong dollar spot weakened to the key support level of HK$7.75 on Thursday from Tuesday's close of HK$7.7477/87. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was heard buying Hong Kong for U.S. dollars to cap the dollar's strength at the key 7.75 level. \par \par \uc2  Steve Gilbert, regional treasurer at First Union National Bank, said "an accumulation of worries" was weighing on the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The Asian crisis is just grinding on. If you look at the local markets, they are just not going anywhere," said Gilbert. \par \par \uc2  Gilbert said investors were also worried about the Chinese yuan. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday for the second time in a week to support the yuan. \par \par \uc2  BA Asia's Gong said a weaker yuan would not necessarily be bad for the Hong Kong dollar because it would make imports from China cheaper. But the market believed a yuan devaluation would weigh heavily on the Hong Kong dollar and imperil its peg to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Investors fear a yuan devaluation could happen quickly, which was why most of the selling of Hong Kong dollars was concentrated in the spot market, said Gong. \par \par \uc2  The HKMA on Wednesday said it was borrowing and buying Hong Kong dollars for the government treasury to fill a seasonal gap in the territory's coffers, not to affect the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was talk the U.S. dollar assets sold for Hong Kong dollars by the HKMA were coming from fiscal rather than exchange fund reserves, which could have a more muted effect on local interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du860219e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
