\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up vs dollar on c. bank buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 06:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 6 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed higher against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Thurady due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at an intraday high of 8.2795 to one dollar from 8.2800 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan weakened early on Thursday in sympathy with the Japanese yen slide on world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the yuan at the 8.2800 level. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the major factor (in Shanghai) today," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lead, domestic banks joined in the buying of the yuan, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to end firmer, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yen stood at 144.85/88 to one dollar at midday in Tokyo from 143.98/08 in late New York on Wednesday due to strong dollar demand and amid weakness in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  This was the second time in a week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to support the yuan. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of China bought the yuan at the same level of 8.2800 per dollar last Friday in keeping with its repeated pledges not to devalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Despite Thursday's gains, dealers said pressure on the yuan to fall was still heavy due to continued weakness of the yen. \par \par \uc2  The yuan was likely to retreat slightly on Friday but it should find support at the key 8.2800 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened at an intraday low of 8.2800 on Thursday, with most business done at 8.2798. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Wednesday was 8.2799. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against Japanese yen at 5.7107 to 100 yen from 5.7480. It ended down against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday low of 1.0689 to one dollar from 1.0680. \par \par \uc2     - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2      - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8601g61\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
