\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar strengthens vs yen by late Tokyo,but capped. \b0\par\par\uc2 673 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0639 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     144.64/69\tab \tab 145.05-143.61\par  USD/DEM     1.7701/06\tab \tab 1.7755-1.7707\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Aug 6 (Reuters) - The dollar extended gains to near \par \par \uc2  145 yen by late Tokyo trade on Thursday as concerns over Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Japanese banking sector fuelled active \par \par \uc2  short-covering and speculative bids, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Rounds of dollar-buying briefly pushed the dollar above 145 \par \par \uc2  yen in the afternoon, but it failed to stay above that level \par \par \uc2  due to a lack of follow-through buying factors. \par \par \uc2  "Speculative forces appear to have driven dollar/yen today," a U.S. bank dealer said. "Short-holders were forced to cover as the dollar unexpectedly climbed from early trade, but the market ran out of incentives to push it further up." \par \par \uc2  Renewed worries about Asia cast a shadow over the yen after speculative sales depressed the Hong Kong dollar amid rumours that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and possibly the Chinese yuan as well, may soon be devalued, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Hong Kong dollar appeared to be moving in tight ranges because the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumoured to be defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently. \par \par \uc2  As of 0659 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar stood at 7.7490/00 per dollar and it moved in a tight range of $7.7495 to $7.7498. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed higher against the dollar due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at an intraday high of 8.2795 to a dollar from 8.28 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong stocks dropped sharply, hurt by a rise in local interbank rates and an easier yen. The Hang Seng Index slid 112.60 points, or 1.51 percent, to close the midsession at 7,353.83. Earlier in the morning it fell to 7,322 points, below its 1998 low of 7,351.68 points. \par \par \uc2  In the afternoon, the yen suffered from heightening concerns over Japan's banking sector amid sharp losses in bank share prices. Rumours that a Japanese bank may be suffering losses in derivatives also hurt the yen, they said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Nikkei average closed 115.94 points, or 0.72 percent, lower at 15,876.22. Banks, which account for about 15 percent of the market's capitalisation, took the brunt of the damage, stock traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Rumours about losses in derivatives sparked a rally in dollar/yen but it brief. The dollar's topside was quite heavy above 145 yen," a commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In the morning, the dollar surged on steady commercial demand at the 0100 GMT fixing. There was talk of large outright purchases worth roughly $800 million by a U.S. investment bank and a Japanese player, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Operators earlier in the morning tried to take the dollar lower against the yen, but they met firm support from Japanese investors and importers, as well as overseas operators. \par \par \uc2  A clear break above 144.40/50 yen, where stop-loss sales were hidden, also intensified the dollar's upward trend. \par \par \uc2  The mark's rebound against the yen indirectly helped provide firm support to dollar/yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The mark regained strength after managing to sustain support at 80.90 yen. A major Asian operator was rumoured to have placed bids to protect its options orders at that level. \par \par \uc2  As of 0717 GMT, the mark stood at 81.74/77 yen compared with 81.35 yen in late New York trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers will pay close attention to the testimony by former White House intern Monica Lewinsky expected later on Thursday, Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi's policy speech and U.S. jobs data both on Friday, to determine the dollar's outlook. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 143.98/08 yen and 1.7700/10 marks in late New York trade on Wednesday. ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8601fnk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
