\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support yuan  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1998\par 08:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday for the second time in a week to support the local yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The move came as worries mount that China will face intense pressure to devalue the yuan to maintain export competitiveness despite its repeated pledges to keep the value of the local unit stable, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the People's Bank of China bought the yuan at 8.2800 against the U.S. dollar on the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System, but they were unable to pinpoint the scope of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for the People's Bank in Beijing declined comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the yuan to close higher at 8.2795 to the dollar from 8.2800 on Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the major factor today," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank bought the yuan at the same level of 8.2800 per dollar last Friday, which showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed to protect that key level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan weakened initially on Thursday in line with a slide in the Japanese yen on world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen stood at 144.85/88 to the dollar at midday in Tokyo, slipping from 143.98/08 in late New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  China has vowed not to devalue the yuan but activity on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  black market in the nation's financial capital of Shanghai has picked up as local citizens hedge their bets. \par \par \uc2  Some black marketeers were quoting a dollar selling rate of 8.90 yuan on Thursday, compared with an official rate of around 8.28 yuan. \par \par \uc2  Shanghai's personal \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits rose 13.2 percent at the end of June from the start of this year to $5.30 billion, as individuals deposited more U.S. dollars to prepare for possible depreciation in the yuan, official media have said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8601c2p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
