\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends steady, market eyes  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1998\par 06:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Aug 3 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed unchanged at 8.2800 to the dollar in cautious trade on Monday after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local unit, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan remained under pressure from a weak Japanese yen on world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets but fears of another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented the local unit from falling below the key 8.2800 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Concerns over further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made traders unwilling to push the yuan below the key level," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of China bought the yuan at the 8.2800 level on Friday to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling below that level. Beijing has repeatedly said it would not devalue the yuan and has vowed to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable. \par \par \uc2  The yen fell to 144.72/74 by midday in Tokyo from 144.60/63 in late New York on Friday, pressured by the yen's losses against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move around the 8.2800 level in the next few days with the negative sentiment from the sagging yen offset by Beijing's pledges to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened at 8.2799 on Monday, moving in a narrow range between an intraday high of 8.2798 and a low of 8.2800 for the entire session. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most business done at 8.2799. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Friday was 8.2799. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the yen at 5.7362 to 100 yen from 5.7700 and it closed little changed against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0682 to one dollar from 1.0680. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8301o0l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
