\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS - Regional  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  ease, stocks mixed. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,102 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 1998\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 31 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended the month on a softer note, with traders here still looking at dollar/yen for direction. \par \par \uc2  Stocks were mixed with the overnight rise on Wall Street boosting some while others were hit by domestic factors and end-month profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  WEAKER YEN HITS REGIONAL \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  And that weak yen is keeping pressure on the downside, although month-end position squaring is providing some support. \par \par \uc2  Japan's new prime minister, Keizo Obuchi, said on Friday he had appointed former senior financial diplomat Toyoo Gyohten as a special adviser to the cabinet to help explain the nation's financial policies to the world. \par \par \uc2  He also said the implementation of six trillion yen in tax cuts and a 10 trillion yen extra budget, which he had previously called for, was a promise to the Japanese people. \par \par \uc2  And he wanted to implement tax cuts as quickly as possible and reckoned the Japanese economy would recover in one to two years, he said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen firmed amid speculation that the new Japanese government was adopting a "benign neglect" stance on the yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan's new finance minister, Kiichi Miyazawa, said the yen and stock prices were basically best left to the market. \par \par \uc2  Some position adjustments did help support some of the regionals but with the exception of the won, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were easier. \par \par \uc2  RUPIAH WILTS DESPITE NEW AID \par \par \uc2  The rupiah sagged despite some bullish news that international donors had promised new loans of $7.9 billion in aid by March. \par \par \uc2  Most of the bullish news had already been priced in earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  This amount comes in addition to a recent six billion dollar loan package from the IMF. \par \par \uc2  The aid is expected to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and many analysts say the official target of 10,000 per dollar looks attainable. \par \par \uc2  CHINA SUPPORTS THE YUAN \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought the yuan at the key 8.2800 level, helping the local unit close at 8.2799 per dollar, little changed from Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan faced fresh pressure on Friday due to renewed falls in the yen," one dealer said. "This triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local unit." \par \par \uc2  Weakness in the yen has sparked fears that China may be forced to devalue the yuan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  RINGGIT FALLS AGAIN \par \par \uc2  In Malaysia, the ringgit is a little softer in thin trade as most commercials have covered their month-end requirements. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said talk of possible snap elections there did nothing to stir the market. \par \par \uc2  Information Minister Mohamad Rahmat told political parties in the ruling coalition to prepare for a snap poll to ensure their mandate in tackling the country's economic woes. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia appeared to be heading towards early polls or a cabinet reshuffle to clip the wings of Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad's deputy, Anwar Ibrahim, market analysts and politicians said. \par \par \uc2  They said that the possibility of general elections was high, but Mahathir might opt for shuffling Anwar out of the finance portfolio while letting him keep the deputy premiership. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the recall of former finance minister Daim Zainuddin into the cabinet in June as minister of special functions had undercut Anwar's position as finance minister. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR SINKS \par \par \uc2  In neighbouring Singapore, the local dollar also eased as jitters over commercial banks' huge exposure to defaulting borrowers grew. \par \par \uc2  Some traders also expressed concern about growing tensions with Malaysia over the shifting of railwaymportant progress," Summers told reporters at an event organised by the U.S. Overseas Private Investment Corp trade agency. \par \par \uc2  But he added: "There is very hard work to do, particularly in the financial sector and in carrying out structural reform." \par \par \uc2  But further reforms are likely to stir up the existing labour problems in the country. \par \par \uc2  THAI STOCKS LOSE EARLY GAINS \par \par \uc2  Thai stocks lost early gains and the baht was lower in late trading. \par \par \uc2  The Labour Ministry said Thai unemployment has reached 2.2 million and the situation is bound to get worse with the current economic crisis. \par \par \uc2  It said 320,000 people had lost their jobs because of collapsing businesses and layoffs, 970,000 were seasonally unemployed and 480,000 were new graduates unable to find jobs. \par \par \uc2  But the figure differs with the Thai National statistics Office, which said recently that unemployment had hit 2.7 million in a work force of 30 million. \par \par \uc2  Asia stock markets started out broadly firmer on Wall Street's overnight bounce but concerns on the weak yen are creeping in. \par \par \uc2  Thailand announced a June balance of payments deficit of $808 million but a May trade surplus of $949 million. \par \par \uc2  Thai foreign reserves at July 24 totalled $27.5 billion. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ..... \par \par \uc2   Change on the day... FRI 31 0921.GMT. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ....Latest.......Prev Close.....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit.....4.14...........4.12...........-0.48% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......12825.00.......12975.00........1.17% \par \par \uc2   Baht........40.85..........40.67..........-0.44% \par \par \uc2   Peso........41.98..........41.99...........0.02% \par \par \uc2   Sing Dlr....1.73...........1.71...........-0.96% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan Dlr..34.37..........34.33..........-0.11% \par \par \uc2   Korean Won..1229.00........1232.00.........0.24% \par \par \uc2   ..... \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis..... \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ....Latest.......July '97.......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit.....4.14...........2.52.........-39.13% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......12825.00.......2432.00......-81.04% \par \par \uc2   Baht........40.85..........25.90........-36.60% \par \par \uc2   Peso........41.98..........26.50........-36.87% \par \par \uc2   Sing Dlr....1.73...........1.43.........-17.17% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan Dlr..34.37..........27.75........-19.26% \par \par \uc2   Korean Won..1229.00........842.00.......-31.49% \par \par \uc2   ************************************************* \par \par \uc2   STOCK MARKETS..... \par \par \uc2   Change on the day... FRI 31 0921.GMT. \par \par \uc2   Market......Current....Prev Close...Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Indonesia....481.72......482.69......-0.2% \par \par \uc2   Malaysia.....402.65......389.53.......3.4% \par \par \uc2   Philippines..1607.61.....1613.50.....-0.4% \par \par \uc2   Singapore....1064.20.....1059.53......0.4% \par \par \uc2   Thailand.....265.04......266.74......-0.6% \par \par \uc2   Hong Kong....7936.20.....7906.16......0.4% \par \par \uc2   Japan........16378.97....16201.60.....1.1% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan.......7653.51.....