\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Crisis At A Glance: LDP Approves Fincl System Measures \b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1998\par 10:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- A key panel of Japan's ruling LDP approved the party's final proposal for financial system stabilization measures, including the creation of a bridge bank. \par \par \uc2  Cheered by news of impending financial system measures, overseas investors are leading a rebound in Tokyo equities, Nihon Keizai Shimbun said. The Nikkei ended up for the seventh straight session. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- Expectations of Japanese banking reform lifted regional stock markets. Hong Kong's index rose 3.8%; the Philippine index ended 4.2% higher; Thailand's index was 4.5% higher; Taiwan's index closed up 3.5% and Singapore's index was up 2.7%. [*R/HK] [*R/RP] [*R/TH] [*R/TW] [*R/SN] \par \par \uc2  -- The dollar rose against the yen on belief that the upcoming Japan announcement on financial system measures won't provide new details. At 0800 GMT, the dollar traded at Y139.17, up from Y137.92 late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Rubin quashed talk of possible joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen, saying the issue hadn't been discussed.  [*R/CH] [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- Senior LDP official Nonaka called for a hike in Japan's official discount rate, currently a record low 0.5%, after July 12 elections, Nihon Keizai Shimbun said. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- An executive of Japan's LDP says the party may extend the period of full protection for bank deposits beyond March 31, 2001, Nihon Keizai Shimbun said. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- Japanese Prime Minister Hashimoto repeated that the LDP would make the income tax system fairer and cut corporate taxes to international levels within three years. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister Tanami played down reports that the government would adopt a permanent tax cut as early as next fiscal year. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy chief said Hong Kong will keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's U.S. dollar peg. [R/HK] \par \par \uc2  -- Moody's said China's financial sector reforms are widening disparities among credit strengths of the country's banks and hurting banking system credit quality. [*R/CH] \par \par \uc2  -- Moody's said the declining asset quality and profits of some Philippine banks may cause rating cuts. [*R/RP] \par \par \uc2  -- Rubin denied backing easier monetary policy in Malaysia, calling into question Prime Minister Mahathir's remarks after a private meeting earlier this week. Rubin said a firm monetary stance was warranted throughout Asia. [*R/MY] \par \par \uc2  Rubin said he sees growing momentum in Asia for reform, which is a recognition generally that reforms are necessary. He said Thailand and Korea are on a sounder path. \par \par \uc2  -- S&P said the ratings outlooks on South Korea's Kookmin Bank, Shinhan Bank, Housing & Commercial Bank and Hana Bank remain negative because of a severe operating environment and Korea's contracting economy. [*R/SK] \par \par \uc2  -- Australian exporters should sell products outside Asia to cut the impact of the region's economic crisis on the domestic economy, a forecasting group said. [*R/ASA] \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-07-98 \par \par \uc2  0850GMT \par \par \uc2  1042 4190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du7205mxi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
