\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  paper sees weak yen despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1998\par 07:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIJING, June 30 (Reuters) - A leading Chinese financial newspaper on Tuesday forecast long-term weakness of the Japanese yen despite the joint U.S.-Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month to lift the slipping \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The yen's exchange rate will obviously experience relatively long-term weakness in the absence of Japanese economic recovery and bearish sentiment on the yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the Financial News said in a commentary. \par \par \uc2  The newspaper is jointly published by the People's Bank of China, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and other major Chinese financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  The newspaper said the U.S.-Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the yen had had just a short-term effect in supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and would not reverse the yen's downward trend. \par \par \uc2  "The yen has once again started falling after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , indicating such a move can only have a short-term effect, although it also showed joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more effective than one-sided action," the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  The yen's weakening fundamentals brought about by a frail Japanese economy and ineffective measures to solve its financial problems remained unchanged, it said. \par \par \uc2  "The slipping yen has triggered renewed financial turmoil in Southeast Asia and had a certain impact on Chinese economic and financial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. President Bill Clinton and his Chinese counterpart Jiang Zemin agreed in a summit meeting last Saturday their countries would do all they could to help crisis-torn Asian economies get back on their feet. \par \par \uc2  But they insisted Japan still held the key to restoring stability in the battered region. \par \par \uc2  While in Beijing, Clinton praised China for its efforts to maintain the value of its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite a steep slide in the Japanese yen that Beijing says has started to hurt its export-driven economy. \par \par \uc2  The yen fell to its lowest level in eight years in recent weeks amid mounting uncertainty over Japan's economic future before the first joint U.S.-Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in more than six years temporarily lifted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value last week. \par \par \uc2  The dollar tumbled below 141 yen in Tokyo Tuesday morning on yen buybacks ahead of the announcement expected later in the week of a "bridge bank" scheme aimed at protecting Japan's ailing financial system. \par \par \uc2  ((Beijing Newsroom (86) 10-6532-1921; Fax (86) 10-6532-4978 \par \par \uc2  beijing.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6u01wcx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
