\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Higher; Mood Bolstered By Clinton's Visit \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1998\par 08:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan firmed against the dollar Tuesday, as sentiment strengthened amid U.S. President Clinton's ongoing visit to China. \par \par \uc2  Global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, fearful that a slide in the yuan may set off a new round of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations, continued to watch the semi-convertible yuan closely. But \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders here said that comments from top U.S. and Chinese officials in support of a stable yuan have helped to bolster sagging confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Others noted that the yuan market was supported by strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of China, which often steps into the market to prevent sharp trading movements. \par \par \uc2  At the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trading Center, the dollar ended Tuesday at 8.2794 yuan (CNY), down from Monday's CNY8.2799. It was traded in a range of CNY8.2794 and CNY8.2799. \par \par \uc2  U.S. President Clinton arrived in Shanghai Monday night and will stay until early Thursday. During a radio show midday Tuesday, he demonstrated ongoing support for Beijing's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy by praising China's moves to maintain a stable yuan. \par \par \uc2  However, Clinton's comments came after trading on China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had ended for the day, and had no effect on the market, market participants said. \par \par \uc2  Gains registered by the Japanese yen against the U.S. dollar Tuesday morning also helped bolster yuan trading during the session, they added. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 30-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0658GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6u05ni2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
