\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends easier vs dollar as yen slides. \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1998\par 06:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 26 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed slightly lower against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Friday, pressured by the sinking Japanese yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But trade was dull ahead of the weekend and recent official statements of support for the yuan kept the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from sustaining bigger losses, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan was hit by renewed weakness in the yen," a dealer said. "But thin trade made the loss of little significance as the yuan remains supported by official pledges not to devalue." \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2797 against the dollar from 8.2796 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The yen eased to 142.55/65 to one dollar at midday, the lowest level since Japan and the United States surprised the market last week by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly to sell dollars. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's fall called in renewed concerns over the yuan's near-term trend," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But the yuan still found firm support at the key 8.2800 level as domestic banks believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the local unit fell below that point," he said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the yuan three times over the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move around the 8.2800 level early next week. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened lower at 8.2799 on Friday, hitting an intraday high of 8.2796 and a low of 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  Most business was done at 8.2798, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Thursday was 8.2799. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the Japanese yen at 5.8032 to 100 yen from 5.8709. It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday high of 1.0685 to one dollar from 1.0692. \par \par \uc2     - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2      - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6q022is\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
