\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up vs dollar on domestic buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1998\par 06:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 25 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed higher against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Thursday, buoyed by a late round of buying by domestic banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The banks, reassured by repeated official pledges to keep the yuan steady, built fresh positions in the last few minutes of trade after the local unit had traded lower for most of the session, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Buying by domestic designated trading banks was the major factor pushing up the yuan today," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at an intraday high of 8.2796 on Thursday from 8.2798 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was still under pressure from renewed weakness of the Japanese yen on world markets. But it held above the key 8.2800 level for most of the session due to the repeated pledges of support from Beijing and the lingering effect of recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen firmed slightly to 140.83/86 against one dollar in Tokyo at midday after slipping below 141.0 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The weak yen limited buying interest in the yuan and that kept the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a narrow range for most of the session," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market three times to support the yuan over the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move around the 8.2800 level on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened at 8.2798 and hit an intraday low of 8.2801. Trade was dull with most business done at 8.2798, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Wednesday was 8.2798. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the Japanese yen at 5.8709 to 100 yen from 5.9001. It ended little changed against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0692 to one dollar from 1.0693. \par \par \uc2     - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2      - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6p0248u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
