\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up marginally against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1998\par 06:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 24 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed up slightly against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Wednesday, brushing aside renewed weakness of the Japanese yen on world markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan found firm support at the key 8.2800 level as sentiment was buoyed by recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in support of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2798 to one dollar on Wednesday from 8.2799 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment towards the yuan was firm mainly due to the lingering effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the local unit," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "This helped the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shrug off renewed weakness of the Japanese yen on the world market." \par \par \uc2  The yen eased to 140 to one dollar in Tokyo by midday on Wednesday against 139.10/15 in New York. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time the dollar hit the 140 level against the yen since the United States and Japan jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 17. \par \par \uc2  The falls in the yen had pressured the yuan over the past few weeks but Beijing had repeatedly said it would not devalue the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times to defend the yuan in the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System in the previous two weeks, helping the yuan hold above the key 8.2800 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was lower at 8.2800 for most of the session on Wednesday but fears of renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented bank traders from trying to breach the key support. \par \par \uc2  "Judging from trading today, the yuan is likely to stay around the (8.2800) level in the near term," another dealer said. "But pressure for the yuan to devalue will mount again if the yen continues to fall." \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened higher at 8.2797 on Wednesday, hitting an intraday high of 8.2796 and a low of 8.2801. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most business done at 8.2797. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Tuesday was 8.2798. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the Japanese yen at 5.9001 to 100 yen from 5.9626. It ended unchanged against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday high of 1.0693 to one dollar. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6o02b2v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
