\par\par \b \uc2  HK stocks open lower in wary trade. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alison Leung \par \uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 1998\par 05:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, June 19 (Reuters) - Hong Kong stocks fell sharply in early Friday trade with the Hang Seng Index losing 156 points, or 1.84 percent, to 8,359 as investors took profits following a strong technical rebound fuelled by a steadier yen. \par \par \uc2  "The Hang Seng Index met some resistance at 8,500 points and is moving down as Japan stocks were also easier this morning," said Peter Lai, associate director, OCBC Securities. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's Nikkei 225-share index lost 156 points, or 1.02 percent, to 15,204 by midday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Short-covering slowed as the Hang Seng has risen more than 1,100 points from the year low of 7,351.68 hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Trading was quiet and the Hang Seng Index was likely to hover around the present levels, Lai said. \par \par \uc2  "The overall trend remains weak but sentiment improved slightly as the downward pressure on the Chinsese yuan became less following a recovery of the yen." \par \par \uc2  Brokers said repeated assurances from Chinese officials that the renminbi would not be devalued also helped soothe nerves. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong reaffirmed on Thursday that China would not devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "It's unnecessary to do that," Dai was quoted by the Xinhua news agency as saying. \par \par \uc2  The yen was likely to stabilise in the short term with investors waiting for results of a new round of discussions on banking reform and tax cuts in Japan, and ahead of U.S. President Bill Clinton's visit to China next week, said Frankie Szeto, analyst at Tai Fook Securities. \par \par \uc2  China-related stocks had surged about 10 percent in response to diminishing worries over yuan devaluation in the short term after the U.S.-Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to support the yen, Szeto said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  plays should continue to outperform the market with defensive and cash-rich red chips as the theme," he added. \par \par \uc2  The red chip index eased two points to 990.72 and the H-share index was down five at 469 points. \par \par \uc2  But China-backed conglomerate China Resources added HK$0.35 at HK$8.55. The company said on Thursday it was looking at five to six projects for possible acquisition. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6j02mcw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
