\par\par \b \uc2  HK stocks open sharply lower in cautious trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 836 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 1998\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, June 19 (Reuters) - Hong Kong stocks fell sharply in early Friday trade with the Hang Seng Index losing 156 points, or 1.84 percent, to 8,359 as investors took profits following a strong technical rebound fuelled by a steadier yen. \par \par \uc2  "The Hang Seng Index met some resistance at 8,500 points and is moving down as Japan stocks were also easier this morning," said Peter Lai, associate director, OCBC Securities. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's Nikkei 225-share index lost 156 points, or 1.02 percent, to 15,204 by midday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Short-covering slowed as the Hang Seng had risen more than 1,100 points from the year low of 7,351.68 hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Trading was quiet and the Hang Seng Index was likely to hover around the present levels, Lai said. \par \par \uc2  "The overall trend remains weak but sentiment improved slightly as the downward pressure on the Chinsese yuan became less following a recovery of the yen." \par \par \uc2  Brokers said repeated assurances from Chinese officials that the renminbi would not be devalued also helped soothe nerves. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong reaffirmed on Thursday that China would not devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "It's unnecessary to do that," Dai was quoted by the Xinhua news agency as saying. \par \par \uc2  The yen was likely to stabilise in the short term with investors waiting for results of a new round of discussions on banking reform and tax cuts in Japan, and ahead of U.S. President Bill Clinton's visit to China next week, said Frankie Szeto, analyst at Tai Fook Securities. \par \par \uc2  China-related stocks had surged about 10 percent in response to diminishing worries over yuan devaluation in the short term after the U.S.-Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to support the yen, Szeto said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  plays should continue to outperform the market with defensive and cash-rich red chips as the theme," he added. \par \par \uc2  The red chip Hang Seng China-Affiliated Corporations Index eased two points to 990.72 and the Hang Seng Chinese Enterprises Index was down five at 469 points. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But China-backed conglomerate China Resources\tab      added HK$0.35 at HK$8.55. The company said on Thursday it was looking at five to six projects for possible acquisition.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Hang Seng Index met some resistance at 8,500 points and is moving down as Japan stocks were also easier this morning," said Peter Lai, associate director, OCBC Securities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo's Nikkei 225-share index lost 156 points, or 1.02 percent, to 15,204 by midday in Tokyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Short-covering slowed as the Hang Seng had risen more than 1,100 points from the year low of 7,351.68 hit on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading was quiet and the Hang Seng Index was likely to hover around the present levels, Lai said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The overall trend remains weak but sentiment improved slightly as the downward pressure on the Chinsese yuan became less following a recovery of the yen."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brokers said repeated assurances from Chinese officials that the renminbi would not be devalued also helped soothe nerves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Dai Xianglong reaffirmed on Thursday that China would not devalue its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "It's unnecessary to do that," Dai was quoted by the Xinhua news agency as saying.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen was likely to stabilise in the short term with investors waiting for results of a new round of discussions on banking reform and tax cuts in Japan, and ahead of U.S. President Bill Clinton's visit to China next week, said Frankie Szeto, analyst at Tai Fook Securities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China-related stocks had surged about 10 percent in response to diminishing worries over yuan devaluation in the short term after the U.S.-Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday to support the yen, Szeto said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  plays should continue to outperform the market with defensive and cash-rich red chips as the theme," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The red chip Hang Seng China-Affiliated Corporations Index eased two points to 990.72 and the Hang Seng Chinese Enterprises Index was down five at 469 points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But China-backed conglomerate China Resources\tab      added HK$0.35 at HK$8.55. The company said on Thursday it was looking at five to six projects for possible acquisition.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par June index futures eased 215 points to 8,375 and July contracts were down 200 points at 8,410.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overall market turnover was HK$1.90 billion after the first hour of trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Legend Holdings\tab      fell HK$0.05 to HK$2.45 despite reporting a net profit of HK$73.27 million for the year ended March 31, 1998, versus a loss of HK$48.64 million a year earlier.\par HSBC Holdings\tab      eased HK$2.50 to HK$185.00 and Hutchison    was down HK$0.60 to HK$37.50, but TVB\tab      rose HK$0.35 to HK$21.35.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Alison Leung (852) 2843 6369; Fax (852) 2845 0636\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Email: hongkong.newsroom@reuters.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par *.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6j02m7t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
