\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan closes unchanged on yen rebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 06:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 18 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed unchanged at 8.2799 against the U.S. dollar on Thursday as overnight rises in the Japanese yen decreased dollar buying in Shanghai, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The yen's rebound on the world markets on Wednesday greatly alleviated dollar buying pressure on the Shanghai market," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan moved in a narrow range between 8.2796 and 8.2800 for the whole session. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of China, stayed on the sidelines, taking no actions to defend the yuan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan had been under heavy downward pressure in the past few weeks due to plunges in the Japanese yen and China's slowing exports, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above the key 8.2800 level since the start of last week, they said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said on Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  welcomed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japan and the United States to support the yen and said a devaluation of the Chinese yuan was not necessary, Xinhua news agency reported. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve and Bank of Japan spent US$6 billion supporting the yen in European and U.S. markets overnight. \par \par \uc2  "We are glad to see that the exchange rate of the Japanese yen is picking up," Xinhua quoted Dai as telling a gathering of Asian bankers in Beijing. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Dai's comments would help sentiment to the local unit and the yuan was likely to continue moving narrowly arround current levels in the short term. \par \par \uc2  Most business was done at 8.2799, Thursday's opening level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against Japanese yen at 6.0750 to 100 yen from 5.7601. It ended little changed against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0700 to one dollar from 1.0702. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02k0x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
