\par\par \b \uc2  HK stocks soar at open on yen moves. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jennifer Genevieve \par \uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 06:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, June 18 (Reuters) - Hong Kong stocks soared at the opening on Thursday after U.S. and Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight to prop up the weak yen brought relief to markets around the region. \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng blue chip index opened on a gain of 6.01 percent at 8,485 points. In China plays, the red chip index jumped 8.11 percent to 965 and the H-share index added 6.09 percent to 458 points. \par \par \uc2  The June futures contract on the Hang Seng Index rocketed to 9,000 points at the opening, a rise of 1,010 points from Wednesday's close. It later pared those gains but was still up 510 points at 8,500. \par \par \uc2  "Right now there is a turnaround in all world markets. This \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been regarded very favourably," said Howard Gorges, a director at South China Brokerage. \par \par \uc2  "Some stocks are up 10 to 20 percent and that is mostly due to short-covering," he said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of Japan jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight selling U.S. dollars for Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar, which rose to an eight year high of above 146 yen earlier in the week, plunged to 136 yen in New York and fell to 135.60 yen in early Asian trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "This is a positive signal to the markets and a hopeful sign for economies in Asia that the U.S. has started to get involved in Japan and that Japan might get on track which would be helpful for the rest of Asia," said Gorges. \par \par \uc2  "The worry recently has been that yen weakness would affect other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including potentially the renminbi. If the renminbi devalued it might bring the Hong Kong dollar down with it. Now people are more relaxed about the stability of the renminbi." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor welcomed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen and said it was unnecessary to devalue the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Fears of a yuan depreciation had hit Hong Kong's China-related stocks hard and the sector roared back on Thursday. New World Infrastructure Ltd led the gainers, soaring HK$2.75, or 34.16 percent, to HK$10.80. \par \par \uc2  The stock had been hit over recent sessions due to concerns about its U.S. dollar debt and renminbi earnings. \par \par \uc2  "China plays will outperform the other stocks as they had been seriously oversold," said Raymond Yin, a director at Core Pacific Asset Management. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6i02k0i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
