\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -5:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Buoys New Taiwan Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 12:21\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Of other Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , both the Indonesian\par rupiah and the Philippine peso came under heavy selling\par pressure Monday.\par    Late in Asia the U.S. dollar was quoted at 14,725 rupiah\par (IDR), up from IDR13,800 Friday. Meanwhile at the close of\par trading on the Philippine Dealing System, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was at 42.450 pesos (PHP), up sharply from PHP40.240 at\par Thursday's close. Philippine markets were closed Friday for a\par public holiday.\par    In north Asia the won ended steeply lower as the South\par Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to track the fall in the yen. At\par the end of trading in the domestic market the U.S. dollar was\par quoted at 1,433 won (KRW), up from KRW1,398.50 at Friday's\par close.\par    The only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  successfully to resist the region-wide\par slide was the new Taiwan dollar, which ended the day higher\par following further vigorous \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , to follow repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actions last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Dealers in Taipei estimated that the authorities sold as\par much as $100 million to suppress the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  below the\par psychologically significant NT$35.00 level.\par    At the close of domestic trading, the U.S. dollar was\par quoted at NT$34.872, down from NT$34.892 at the end of\par Friday's session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  06-15-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0621EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du6f01fwm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
