\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  yuan ends down vs dollar, c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 1998\par 05:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 12 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed down slightly against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Friday as sentiment remained weak over China's poor foreign trade data in May, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the yuan from falling sharply, supporting the local unit firmly above the key 8.2800 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2799 to one dollar on Friday from 8.2796 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan was still under the pressue of China's slowing exports," a dealer said. "But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying the yuan just above the key 8.2800 level, preventing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling sharply." \par \par \uc2  The official Xinhua news agency said on Wednesday that China's exports fell 1.5 percent year-on-year in May, the first such decline in 22 months, mainly due to the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan was also pressured by the plunging Japanese yen, which had caused speculation that the local unit could be devalued. \par \par \uc2  Beijing has repeatedly said it would not devalue the local unit despite the recent steep depreciation of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  China will stick to its decision not to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the weakness of the Japanese yen, China's Foreign Trade Minister Shi Guangsheng said on Thursday in Brussels. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan would move in a narrow range around the 8.2800 level next week with the impact of slowing exports and falling Japanese yen offset by Beijing's determination to defend the yuan. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the yuan opened down at an intraday low of 8.2800 and hit an intraday high of 8.2794. Most business was done at around 8.2798, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Thursday was 8.2798. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against Japanese yen at 5.7561 to 100 yen from 5.8430, continuing an upward trend in recent weeks due to the yen's weakness on the world markets, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0696 to one dollar from 1.0705. \par \par \uc2      - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2      - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6c037ou\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
