\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support yuan. \b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 1998\par 08:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 12 (Reuters) - Worried by a weakening Japanese yen and bearish trade data, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Friday for the second time this week to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of China, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would continue to support the yuan at above the key 8.2800 level against the U.S. dollar on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought whenever the yuan approached the key 8.2800 level," a dealer in Shanghai said. \par \par \uc2  The bank has been defending the 8.2800 level but \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were rare in the past few months, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought the yuan for what dealers said was the first time in months after the local unit hit a six-month closing low of 8.2805 last week. \par \par \uc2  They saw yuan buying from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though not in big volumes, on Friday again when the local unit touched an intra-session low of 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  "The (yuan) buying was not heavy today because it's easy to support the yuan in a quiet market ahead of the weekend," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment. The Shanghai-based market, the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System, does not post trading volumes. \par \par \uc2  The Chinese yuan ended Friday at 8.2799 against Thursday's 8.2796. Friday, the local unit moved in a 8.2800-8.2794 range. \par \par \uc2  "The yuan was still under the pressure of China's slowing exports," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The outlook for the Chinese yuan, which has been under pressure from poor foreign trade data, has been dampened further by the weak Japanese yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Trade data released on Wednesday showing Chinese export growth slowed in May for the first time in 22 months added to worries about whether the yuan would cave in. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen hit a nearly eight-year low of 144.75 to the dollar in Tokyo on Friday morning after U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said the only cure to the yen's weakness was restoring economic growth in Japan. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in New York said the Bank of China had been a sporadic buyer of Japanese yen against the dollar in recent days and weeks. \par \par \uc2  Bank of China has also been a frequent seller of U.S. treasury bills, fuelling speculation that the bank may be using some dollar reserves to support the yen, the dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A Bank of China official in New York said the bank was not involved in any such dealings. \par \par \uc2  Beijing has repeatedly said it would not devalue the local unit despite the recent steep depreciation of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Zhu Bangzao called on Japan on Thursday to show "courage and wisdom" to halt the yen's slide and insisted China's policy of not devaluing its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained unchanged. \par \par \uc2  China's Foreign Trade Minister Shi Guangsheng said on Thursday in Brussels that China would stick to its decision not to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the weakness of the Japanese yen. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2  - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6c02x7y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
