\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends down against dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1998\par 06:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 9 (Rse yuan closed down against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Tuesday amid worries that China's exports might slow down, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 8.2799 to one dollar against 8.2795 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The market widely expected slower foreign trade for the first five months of this year, dealers said. Beijing is scheduled to announce the data in mid-June. \par \par \uc2  China's exports grew by 11.6 percent in the first four months of this year, but the growth was slower than 27.9 percent for the whole 1997 mainly due to the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  "Traders believed the January-May trade data would indicate slower exports," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "This would mean slower inflows of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and would hurt China's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves," he said. \par \par \uc2  But the yuan, which has been in a slight downward trend in the past few weeks, is supported by official pledges not to devalue the local unit. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Monday to prevent the yuan from falling, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is likely to move narrowly around the 8.2800 level in the next few days due to official support, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the yuan opened lower at 8.2798, hitting an intraday high of 8.2790 and a low of 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most business done at 8.2798. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2798. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against Japanese yen at 5.8741 to 100 yen from Monday's 5.8901, continuing an upward trend due to the yen's weakness on the world markets. \par \par \uc2  It ended down against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0693 to one dollar from 1.0690. \par \par \uc2      - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2      - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6903gjp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
