\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  yuan ends little changed on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 1998\par 06:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, June 8 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed little changed against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Monday due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the local unit from falling, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of China bought the yuan late in the session when the local unit touched the key 8.2800 support level, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented the yuan from falling and made it close little changed," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2795 to one dollar on Monday from 8.2794 last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in line with recent official pledges to keep the yuan steady. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a rare move in recent months," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "It indicated the central government's intention not to allow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depreciate, at least in the short term," he said. "This should give the yuan some support." \par \par \uc2  The yuan had recently been pressured by China's slowing exports and foreign investment inflows, as well as weakness in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the regional financial crisis, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move just above the 8.2800 level in the new few days on the strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's support on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened unchanged at an intraday high of 8.2794 on Monday and hit a low of 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most business done at 8.2796. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Friday was 8.2794. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against Japanese yen at 5.8901 to 100 yen from 5.9600. It ended down against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0690 to HK$1 from 1.0682. \par \par \uc2      - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015 \par \par \uc2      - Email: reutersh@uninet.com.cn \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6803dh1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
