\par\par \b \uc2  China  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  resumes open market  \highlight22\uc2 operations \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 02:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BEIJING, June 5 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has resumed open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through repurchase agreements in the money market to meet the capital needs of commercial banks, the Financial News daily said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The paper quoted unnamed officials in the People's Bank of China as saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  began on May 26. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April 1996 through debt repurchase agreement to help adjust money supply. \par \par \uc2  It had suspended the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the beginning of last year mainly because of lacklustre trading, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had focused on recalling loans from commercial banks as the main lever to control rising money supply released through the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, it said. \par \par \uc2  Money supply was fuelled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 China Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System to prevent the yuan from depreciating before the Asian financial crisis broke out. \par \par \uc2  China's economic and financial situation had changed this year after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrapped quotas on loans for commercial banks, reformed the reserve ratio system and lowered interest rates, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  The newspaper quoted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials as saying the growth in deposits of commercial banks had slowed and steps needed to be taken to meet their capital requirements. \par \par \uc2  In order to increase the flexibility and effectiveness of monetary policy management the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through debt repurchase agreement, it said. \par \par \uc2  The move was also part of the drive by the government to ensure its targeted 8.0 percent economic growth this year and maintain the stable exchange rate of the yuan, the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would trade debt repurchase agreements with 25 primary dealers including major commercial banks, it said. \par \par \uc2  In the near future, the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  would focus on releasing funds to commercial banks from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has started from Wednesday issuing information on trading, including interest rates, it said, without giving further details. \par \par \uc2  - Beijing Newsroom (86) 10-6532-1921; Fax (86) 10-6532-4978 \par \par \uc2  - Email: beijing.newsroom@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6503i36\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
