\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Up: PBOC Dlr Selling Counters Wed.s Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1998\par 07:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--China's yuan ended a touch higher against the U.S. dollar Thursday in stable trading held steady by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yuan is tradable under the current account only. Its market movements are strictly controlled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank Of China, or PBoC, which allows the yuan to trade against the dollar only within certain limits. \par \par \uc2  At the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trading Center, the dollar closed at CNY8.2791, down from Wednesday's CNY8.2805. It traded between CNY8.2791 and CNY8.2800, with most transactions concentrated around CNY8.2799. \par \par \uc2  According to one market participant, trade Thursday was stable "with a good balance of dollar supply and demand in the market." \par \par \uc2  Recently, concerns that China may soon be forced to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - in order to maintain export competitiveness - have pressured the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. On Wednesday, the yuan broke a psychological level, ending the day at CNY8.2805 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  But strong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows - most of which must be converted to yuan - and large \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which bolster the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are keeping the yuan strong. \par \par \uc2  As a result of its strong fundamentals and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan's trading movements remain slight, changing only a fragment of a percentage point during trade each day. \par \par \uc2  In other trading Thursday, the Hong Kong dollar closed at CNY1.0685, down from Wednesday's CNY1.0690 while the Japanese yen ended at CNY5.9880 per 100 yen, up from the previous close of CNY5.9563. \par \par \uc2  In the non-deliverable forward market, which gives an indication of how participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade in the coming few months, money broker Exco Group in Singapore on Thursday was quoting the U.S. dollar at CNY8.6200 for delivery in six months and at CNY8.9900 over a one-year timeframe. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As well as being only semi-convertible, the yuan is controlled by\par tight trading margins for the yuan, both with official price limits for\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a strong trading presence by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par stabilize even slight fluctuations.\par by Catherine McKinley; (8621)6279-7294; cmckinley@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0557GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6404rks\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
