\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. dollar swaps soften at front end again. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Apu Sikri \par \uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 1998\par 22:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 28 (Reuters) - The short end of U.S. dollar swaps softened for the third consecutive session with two-year and three-year swaps losing a whole basis point. \par \par \uc2  The two-year spread dipped to 34.5 basis points over the outstanding note and 36.25 basis points over the when-issued note. The three-year spread dropped to 39.5 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have a new and rather intriguing explanation for the softening: short-maturity Treasuries are being pressured by worries that Japan and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  could dump these notes to raise funds for potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - Japan to support the yen and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support a weakening Hong Kong dollar. Hong Kong maintains a \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it could theoretically draw on China's reserves to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In any case, the fear that any number of foreign central banks holding the largest chunk of U.S. Treasuries could dump them to raise cash is prompting Treasuries to underperform Eurodollar futures and in turn widening the Treasury-Eurodollar (TED) spread and the swap spread. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the five-year swap spread dipped to 41.5 basis points with the roll to the newly auctioned note inverted by two basis points. Dealers generally preadjust the swap spread to the new note and discount for the fact that the swap spread may not adjust to the full extent of the roll. \par \par \uc2  At the long end, the seven-year swap spread closed at 46.5 basis points and the 10-year at 52.75 basis points. The term-repo on the 10-year note continues to hover around 3 percent. \par \par \uc2  (( - N.A. Treasury Desk; 212 859-1660 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5s044w1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
