\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends little changed,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, May 5 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed little changed against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped early gains backed by news that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had opened its interbank market to foreign banks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2786 to one dollar on Tuesday from 8.2787 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Eight foreign banks which have already been licensed to take yuan deposits had been permitted to join the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  interbank market to trade yuan, bonds and repurchase agreements, the China Securities News reported on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to remain stable below the 8.2780 level on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened at 8.2785 and moved up to an intraday high of 8.2779 early in trading. It then fell slowly for the rest of the session, touching a low of 8.2787. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2785. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against the Japanese yen at 6.2340 to 100 yen from 6.2145. It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday low of 1.0685 to one dollar from 1.0690. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom (86) 21-6355-4009; Fax 21-6355-5015. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5505zra\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
