\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Lower Vs Dlr On Strong Dollar Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1998\par 07:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--The yuan ended slightly lower against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, with another day of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pinned in a narrow range, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trading Center, the dollar closed at CNY8.2790, up from Tuesday's CNY8.2789. It traded in a range CNY8.2788 and CNY8.2796. \par \par \uc2  The yuan, still tradable under the current account only, has traded in an extremely tight range for the last few weeks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been cited as actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in order to prevent any appearance that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be under pressure to decline. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are part of the central government's pledge to boost regional stability by not to depreciating the yuan in the wake of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declines. \par \par \uc2  Traders generally say that strong capital inflows from the country's large trade surplus and still-strong foreign-investment inflows are keeping the yuan under pressure to gain. But new dollar buying pressure, in part from foreign-trade companies and in part from smaller financial institutions fearing a weaker yuan, has emerged in recent sessions, the participants note. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar open strong and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market immediately to support the yuan,' said a trader with a state bank. He noted confidence in the dollar is strong, and that many expect the yuan to weaken gradually in coming months. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 04-03-98 \par \par \uc2  0620GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du3401w7s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
