\par\par \b \uc2  Yuan ends little changed vs US dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 22 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed little changed against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Thursday with active buying of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  being offset by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Yuan demand rose ahead of Lunar New Year, with domestic banks and enterprises keen to settle accounts, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2786 to one dollar on Thursday from 8.2787 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Despite renewed plunges by Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bidding for the yuan was active and that strengthened pro-yuan sentiment," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The gains were capped by the cental bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not fully convertible on the capital account. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's rupiah continued to hit record lows on Thursday morning, prompting Jakarta's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to takes steps to bring it back up to 13,500 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Local dealers said that as domestic banks were expected to buy more local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet increasing demand ahead of next week's New Year holiday, the yuan was likely to move above the 8.2785 level on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened at 8.2785 and moved around 8.2784 for most of the session, hitting an intraday low of 8.2792 and a high of 8.2782. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Wednesday was 8.2786. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against the Japanese yen at 6.5201 to 100 yen from 6.4400. It ended down against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0708 to one dollar from 1.0681. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai Newsroom (86) -21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1m0400b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
