\par\par \b \uc2  China Yuan Ends Lower Vs Dlr On Technical Correction \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1998\par 06:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI (Dow Jones)--The yuan ended lower against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, falling on a technical correction after six consecutive advances for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  They added, however, that capital inflows were again strong, and that the yuan is likely to come under more pressure to gain in coming sessions. \par \par \uc2  At the Shanghai-based China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trading Center, the dollar closed at CNY8.2790, up from Tuesday's CNY8.2788. It traded in a range of CNY8.2787 and CNY8.2794. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is watching trade closely, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable as part of efforts to diffuse market concern that China may devalue its unit to keep pace with Asia. \par \par \uc2  Concern has been mounting among domestic individuals of a yuan devaluation, despite repeated vows from top Chinese government officials that it won't happen. \par \par \uc2  The yuan is still convertible under the current account only, leaving it unscathed by the ongoing regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. The controls on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also mean that a devaluation would be government engineered, and not based on market forces. \par \par \uc2  In other trading Wednesday, the Hong Kong dollar closed at CNY1.0702, up from Tuesday's close of CNY1.0700, while the Japanese yen ended at CNY6.3088 per Y100, up from the previous close of CNY6.2231. \par \par \uc2  In the non-deliverable forward market, which gives an indication of how participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade in the coming few months, money broker Exco Group in Singapore on Wednesday was quoting the U.S. dollar at CNY9.1794 yuan for delivery in six months and at CNY10.2794 over a one-year timeframe. \par \par \uc2  In addition to being only semiconvertible, the yuan is controlled by tight trading margins, with both official price limits for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a strong trading presence stabilizing even slight fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  The high NDF rates, however, suggest that some banks are betting on a weaker yuan. \par \par \uc2  -By Karby Leggett; 86 21 6279-7294; kleggett@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  14-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0513GMT \par \par \uc2  1153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914du1e0065d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
