\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends down against dollar in Shanghai. \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 14 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed slightly lower against the dollar on Wednesday on profit-taking after gains over the past two days, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan met resistance when it neared its closing high of 8.2785 set in May 1995 and the failure to breach the level triggered profit-taking, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Profit-taking set in after the yuan failed to breach the 8.2785 level on Wednesday," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2790 to one dollar on Wednesday from 8.2788 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were concerned the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depress the yuan as it approached the 8.2785 level. \par \par \uc2  "Buyers seemed unwilling to push the yuan higher due to those concerns," another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Chinese yuan has moved higher in the past few months despite the weakening of many Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the regional financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  China's strong economic fundamentals coupled with repeated official statements that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be devalued were helping to buoy the yuan, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move around the 8.2790 level on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the yuan opened at 8.2790 and held to a narrow range around the opening price for most of the session. It hit an intraday low of 8.2794 and a high of 8.2787. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active with most business done at 8.2790. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Tuesday was 8.2790. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed down against the Japanese yen at 6.3088 to 100 yen from 6.2231. It ended down slightly against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday low of 1.0703 to one dollar from 1.0700. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1e07z6z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
