\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends up vs dollar despite  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed higher against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday on the back of increased demand from domestic banks ahead of the Chinese Lunar New Year festival, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bought dollars but its modest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  merely capped the yuan's rise, keeping the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  below the 8.2785 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2788 to one dollar on Tuesday from 8.2792 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Domestic banks bought the yuan, anticipating demand from enterprises ahead of the New Year," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  Chinese New Year is traditionally a time for the settling of accounts. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said as the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was not exposed to foreign speculative funds, it is still stable. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in modest amounts when the yuan neared the (8.2785 level)," another dealer said. "This put some buyers of the yuan on the retreat." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to turn lower on Wednesday after today's gains. \par \par \uc2  The yuan opened at 8.2794 and touched an intraday low of 8.2795 early in the session. It then rose to move around 8.2790 for the remainder of the day, hitting a high of 8.2761. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Monday was 8.2794. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the Japanese yen at 6.2231 to 100 yen from 6.2630. It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0700 to one dollar from 1.0710. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom (86) -21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du1d07xcj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
