\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends little changed against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 18 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed almost unchanged against the U.S. dollar in Shanghai on Thursday following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising sharply, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed to prevent the yuan from breaching the historical closing high of 8.2785 set in May 1995, the highest since the market opened in 1994, they said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying dollars to prevent the yuan from breaching the record closing high," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed at 8.2791 to one dollar on Thursday from 8.2793 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Trading was active with most business done at about 8.2791. \par \par \uc2  Despite Thursday's consolidation, dealers said bullish sentiment for the yuan was little affected due to an oversupply of dollars on the market on the back of China's surging foreign trade surplus and steady foreign investment inflows. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody thinks the yuan has downside space in the near term," a second dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move around the current level on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The yuan on Thursday opened unchanged at 8.2793 and stuck to a narrow range just below the 8.2790 level for most of the session, hitting an intraday high of 8.2789 and a low of 8.2797, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price on Wednesday was 8.2791. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed up against the Japanese yen at 6.4800 to 100 yen from 6.5000. \par \par \uc2  It ended slightly down against the Hong Kong dollar at 1.0686 to one dollar from 1.0684. \par \par \uc2  -- Shanghai Newsroom (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtci00yhn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
