\par\par \b \uc2  China yuan ends little changed vs US dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SHANGHAI, Dec 8 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan closed little changed against the U.S. dollar on Monday as bullish sentiment towards the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was offset by fears over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank traders kept to the sidelines amid concern the People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yuan's advance as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved around the 8.2800 level last week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Jitters over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented the yuan from rising despite bullish sentiment," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The yuan ended at 8.2799 to one dollar from 8.2800 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Trading was dull with most business done at 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yuan had little room to fall due to an oversupply of dollars on the market and Beijing's recent pledge not to allow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depreciate. \par \par \uc2  China's top economic strategist Zhu Rongji was quoted as saying there was no need to let the yuan fall to spur exports despite the recent weakening of Southeast Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the yuan to move around 8.2800 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the yuan opened at 8.2799 and moved in a narrow range of its intraday high of 8.2790 and 8.2800 for most of the session. It touched a low of 8.2849. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average price last Friday was 8.2800. \par \par \uc2  The yuan closed little changed against the Japanese yen at 6.3897 to 100 yen from 6.3900. \par \par \uc2  It ended up against the Hong Kong dollar at an intraday high of 1.0708 to one dollar from 1.0712. \par \par \uc2  - Shanghai Newsroom: (86) 21-6279-7004; Fax 21-6279-7174 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc801gc3\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (china near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw)and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\b